James decides to run 3 sprints 3 times a week.  He runs 60 meters each sprint.  How many total meters does he run a week? Solve briefly and end with 'Answer: <number>'.
model
<|channel>thought
*   Sprints per session: 3
    *   Sessions per week: 3
    *   Distance per sprint: 60 meters

    *   Total sprints per week = (Sprints per session) × (Sessions per week)
    *   Total sprints per week = 3 × 3 = 9
    *   Total distance per week = (Total sprints per week) × (Distance per sprint)
    *   Total distance per week = 9 × 60

    *   9 × 60 = 540

    *   3 sprints/session * 3 sessions/week = 9 sprints/week
    *   9 sprints/week * 60 meters/sprint = 540 meters/week

